From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:48:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(open-items): record items an agent labels only in chat,
 and tell it

Agents with the open items tools are asked to record every item with
sys_open_items_raise, but they still often write [Q3] **Title** detail in
chat without it. Such an item is missing from the store, the panel and
sys_open_items_list, and a later tool raise can collide with its number.

After each turn ends, off the turn's path, the server reads the agent
messages written since it last looked (first time: the latest turn only,
nothing older is backfilled) with the chat's own label rules, ported once
to omnigent/entities/item_labels.py and tested against the same cases as
the web parser (web/src/lib/__fixtures__/itemLabelCases.json):

- a label the store lacks, written where an item starts, is recorded
  under that label (raised_by "auto") with its title, block and links; a
  link label stores its first link;
- a struck label closes its item if it is still open (closed_by "auto",
  the striking sentence as the resolution);
- labels the store has are left alone, so retries, re-reads and edits add
  nothing and no tool label is taken; a later tool raise of a recorded
  label takes the item over and keeps its number. The session cap holds,
  and one read changes at most 20 labels.

When a read changed something, the agent's next message carries one
framework notice, e.g. '[Open items] Q3 "Region?" was labelled in chat
without being recorded, so it was added for you. Next time record items
with sys_open_items_raise; set a topic or close them with
sys_open_items_update if needed. Open now: 4.', at most three per session.
The instruction does not mention any of this, so agents keep using the
tool. A new side-store revision (open_items0002) keeps the per-session
read position and the untold changes.

Not proposed upstream yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
